    {
      "kind": "dealer",
      "url": "https://thomannmusic.com/mackie_profx12v3.htm",
      "note": "Thomann ProFX12v3 page (opened 2026-11-12): 102 x 330 x 376 mm (H x W x D), 3.6 kg; 7 mic inputs (channels 1-2 combo with Hi-Z), 5 mono line inputs, 4 stereo inputs, one 3.5 mm stereo input, USB-B (the page says 4 in / 2 out in one place and 2 in / 4 out in another), one footswitch input, an XLR master output, 2 aux / monitor outputs, one headphone jack, 48 V phantom. The mains inlet (3-pin IEC line cord) and the 1/4 in main and sub outputs come from the Mackie ProFXv3+ specification sheet and the knowledge base (the v3+ sheet read as text: 102 x 330 x 376 mm, 3.6 kg, the same footprint); the plan treats the v3 as the same footprint. MODELLED SUBSET (documented): 7 mic XLR inputs, the 3.5 mm stereo input, the main XLR L / R, the monitor and FX sends, 2 sub outs, the headphone jack, the footswitch, USB-B and the IEC inlet (18 ports); the 1/4 in line inputs of the mono and stereo channels, the inserts and the direct outs are not modelled. Positions are GUESSES: the real unit has its channel inputs on the top rear panel, here every connector sits on the rear face (no drawing was read). The profile is an estimate: the sources give the three outer sizes only, the sheet drawings were not readable as text."
    },
    {
      "kind": "datasheet",
      "url": "https://mackie.com/img/file_resources/PROFXV3+_SERIES_SS.pdf",
      "note": "Mackie ProFXv3+ series specification sheet (read as text): ProFX12v3+ 4.0 x 13.0 x 14.8 in = 102 x 330 x 376 mm, 7.9 lb = 3.6 kg; 1/4 in and XLR main outputs, 1/4 in sub outputs, aux outputs, USB 2.0 (2 in 4 out), stereo 1/8 in input, headphone output, 3-pin IEC line cord."
    }
  ]
